Marcus Wilbanks
We used the Titanic dataset to examine passenger records and figure out who managed to
survive a disaster.
I ran my own plots to see how the port and passenger fares correlated with survival.
Creating a boxplot for fares showed that survivors generally paid significantly higher ticket
prices, aligning neatly with the class disparities we found previously.
The gender distribution was checked and confirmed a spike in female survivorship . The
age histograms showed a concentration of children among the survivors.
This taught me about EDA and that data is very important to ML. There is not a part I like
more than the other, I simply just like learning about new things.
